PATCH 241: DWORD (uint*) casts on FUN_0000_6250's RESOURCE-archive header/directory derefs of DAT_623c
(asm-verified vs re_out/fist_image.bin; completes what PATCH 237's description promised).

THE DETERMINISM ROOT of the collapsed in-mission colormap (uniform terrain).  DAT_623c is assembled as
`undefined1*` (byte pointer -- deliberately, for the twin 62fd byte path), but 6250 reads the PAL.RES
archive HEADER magic and the member COUNT as 32-bit dwords (asm 62d0 `lods eax`; 16-byte directory entry
stride).  Ghidra typed DAT_623c `uint*` in these expressions, so once the assemble macro made it byte*,
`*DAT_623c` read ONE BYTE (0x52='R') and the compare `== 0x4f534552` ('RESO') NEVER matched -> the
'RESO'/'URCE' magic check failed DETERMINISTICALLY -> the 532.pal member was never resolved -> 6032's
5598 palette stayed empty -> the 9e60/ac70 colormap remap LUT collapsed to a single index -> the op-0x0c
voxel render drew a UNIFORM terrain.  (NB: this is NOT the "623c overwrite" the prior notes hypothesised
-- the header read is always byte-correct 'RESOURCE1'; the defect is the byte-vs-dword deref width.)

PATCH 237 fixed the AH=3F buffer ADDRESS (EDX32 = full DAT_623c pointer, not the low-16 SUB42) and its
header CLAIMS "localized (uint*) casts for 6250 only", but its committed diff OMITS them.  241 supplies
exactly those casts on the direct DAT_623c dword derefs (the member-match walk already goes through the
uint* locals puVar9/puVar10, which now initialise correctly).  RUNTIME-VERIFIED: magic passes, directory
reads (count=32), member resolves (find_cf=0, size=768), 5598 loads 524/768 nonzero, and op-0x0c renders
colormap distinct=31 / fb-colors=18 -- STABLE every run (no longer heap/tick-dependent).  Cascade-only
(reached only via the op-0x18 mission map-load) -> BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 menu/dialog flows.
Source pristine; fist_ext.c via build/.  Portable C.
